<!-- vaml_viewer — Sprint 11ac VIEWER-GROWTH sample (dep:S829, Sprint 11ac): THE
     CORRECTED MEASURE SEMANTICS RENDERED LIVE. The three S827/S828/S829
     closures all resolve + render through the generic renderer (the S222_1 /
     11k-6 RELOAD re-demonstrated — proving NO regression from the S827/S828/
     S829 measure-math changes).

     Ground truth (E:\GitRepos\wpf, read directly — quoted, not assumed):

       * FrameworkElement.cs:4284-4500 MeasureCore — `Size unclippedDesiredSize
         = desiredSize;` (4394) is the content extent; the over-constrained arm
         clamps it to `availableSize` ("In overconstrained scenario, parent wins
         and measured size of the child … can not be larger then available
         size. We will clip the guy later.", 4435-4450) and returns the CLAMPED
         pair as `DesiredSize` while keeping `UnclippedDesiredSizeField`
         (4473-4491). See the [WPF DIVERGENCE] note below: VAML's
         `desired_size()` is WPF's UnclippedDesiredSize, not its DesiredSize.

       * FrameworkElement.cs:4507-4690 ArrangeCore — `arrangeSize` starts from
         the slot, GROWS to `unclippedDesiredSize` and sets `NeedsClipBounds`
         when the slot is smaller (4579-4599); `Alignment != Stretch` arranges
         at the unclippedDesiredSize (4617-4623); `effectiveMaxWidth =
         Math.Max(unclippedDesiredSize.Width, mm.maxWidth)` caps a Stretch
         ("Clipping by Max is needed to limit stretch here", 4636-4655).

       * Stack.cs:738-757 StackArrangeHelper — NO last-child branch: every child
         gets `rcChild.Width = child.DesiredSize.Width` (stacking axis) and
         `Math.Max(arrangeSize.Axis, child.DesiredSize.Axis)` (cross axis). The
         Stretch FILL is the CHILD's ArrangeCore, not the panel's.

       * UIElement.cs:561-700 Measure — reentrancy guard, `Visibility.Collapsed`
         skip (601-611, keeps the dirty bit + re-arms `_previousAvailableSize`),
         clean early-out (648-651), `InvalidateArrange()` on every real pass
         (626, "we always want to be arranged, ensure arrange request"), and the
         DesiredSize-changed waterfall to the parent (687-700).

       * UIElement.cs:2938-2954 / 2976-3034 — Visibility is a plain
         `PropertyMetadata` (NOT AffectsMeasure) whose change callback runs
         `switchVisibilityIfNeeded` → `ensureVisible`/`ensureInvisible` →
         `signalDesiredSizeChange()` on both Collapsed edges;
         UIElement.cs:323-330 `OnChildDesiredSizeChanged` defaults to
         `if (IsMeasureValid) InvalidateMeasure();`.

     The LIVE window display is the [both-apps, not CI] on-machine gate; the
     SEAM (vaml_viewer/viewer_growth_11ac.h + its headless test) is the
     CI-checkable half of the exact code path. ADR-021 consumer path.
     NO MINIMAL REAL. ADR-018 ZERO new locks.
-->

<!-- ===========================================================================
     [WPF DIVERGENCE] REGISTER (the NO-GAP sibling of the MINIMAL REAL marker: a
     known, scheduled, SEARCHABLE difference from the WPF source — recorded here
     so it can never be silently backfilled or mistaken for WPF-true)

       [WPF DIVERGENCE] #1 the single DesiredSize store — desired_size() IS
       WPF's `UnclippedDesiredSize` (FrameworkElement.cs:4394, 4473-4491); WPF
       keeps a CLAMPED parent-facing DesiredSize beside it
       (FrameworkElement.cs:4435-4450) — RESOLVED BY S832 (Sprint 11ad).
       Do NOT paper over; do NOT assert as WPF-true.

       [WPF DIVERGENCE] #2 no `NeedsClipBounds` / `GetLayoutClip` — WPF marks a
       squeezed element and clips it against the smaller slot
       (FrameworkElement.cs:4579-4599, 4874; UIElement.cs:3322-3333) —
       RESOLVED BY S833 (Sprint 11ad). Do NOT paper over; do NOT assert as
       WPF-true.

       [WPF DIVERGENCE] #3 `compute_final_rect` pins a non-Stretch child to
       min(inner, avail) instead of arranging it at its unclipped desired size,
       and there is no `effectiveMaxWidth/Height` arrange cap
       (FrameworkElement.cs:4617-4623, 4636-4655) — RESOLVED BY S832 (Sprint
       11ad). Do NOT paper over; do NOT assert as WPF-true.

       [WPF DIVERGENCE] #4 `StackPanel::ArrangeOverride` gives the LAST child a
       leftover track (`isLast ? remaining : desired`, Element.cpp:2613-2640)
       and offers the panel's own width as the cross-axis slot; WPF's
       `StackArrangeHelper` has NO last-child branch and uses
       `Math.Max(arrangeSize.Axis, child.DesiredSize.Axis)` (Stack.cs:738-757) —
       RESOLVED BY S1239 (Sprint 11ca, D1). Do NOT paper over; do NOT assert as
       WPF-true.
     =========================================================================== -->

<StackPanel xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
            x:Name="Root" Width="640" Height="520" Margin="6"
            Background="#F0F0F0">
  <TextBlock Text="11ac — the corrected measure semantics render live"
             FontSize="16" Margin="4"/>

  <!-- Closure A (S827 — DesiredSize-bounds): a child whose CONTENT exceeds its
       offered slot must still report its wider content. WideText is a single
       40-character unbreakable token: default_text_metric advance is 0.6 ×
       FontSize = 7.2 DIPs, so the line measures 40 × 7.2 = 288 DIPs wide — one
       line, no mid-word break (TextLayout.cpp:296-310, "a word LONGER than the
       full avail still gets its own line (overflows rather than wraps
       mid-word)"). The panel offers it a 120-wide slot (SqueezePanel's Width),
       so DesiredSize (288) EXCEEDS the offer — WPF's "soft constraint"
       (UIElement.cs:541-551).

       The MEASURE half asserted here IS WPF-true: MeasureOverride's output is
       content + margin, never clamped to `available`. The ARRANGE half is
       divergence #1/#3 in the register at the foot of this header (S832). -->
  <StackPanel x:Name="SqueezePanel" Width="120" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
              Margin="4" Background="#E0E0E0">
    <TextBlock x:Name="WideText" FontSize="12"
               Text="WWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWW"/>
  </StackPanel>

  <!-- Closure B (S828 — the Stretch/Fill pass): alignment is an ARRANGE-only
       concern. Both probes are authored IDENTICALLY (Height=40, no Width, Fill
       only), so they present the SAME measure input; the ONLY difference is
       HorizontalAlignment. StretchChild (default Stretch) is arranged at the
       panel's whole 300-wide cross-axis (its own ArrangeCore Stretch arm,
       FrameworkElement.cs:4597-4620, "Alignment==Stretch --> arrange at the
       slot size minus margins"), while LeftChild is arranged at its
       unclippedDesiredSize (FrameworkElement.cs:4617-4623) — the measure pass
       never saw the alignment at all.
       Two children, so the non-last slot is exercised and the cross-axis result
       cannot come from a last-child filler (WPF Stack.cs:738-757 has no such
       branch at all).
       The UNBOUNDED axis is the panel's stacking axis: the vertical StackPanel
       offers `Size::Infinite().height` (S129), so a Stretch child is measured
       at content height — never "wrapped" into the infinite offer (the removed
       invented "Stretch + infinite → wrap" branch). -->
  <StackPanel x:Name="StretchPanel" Width="300" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
              Margin="4" Background="#E8E8E8">
    <Rectangle x:Name="StretchChild" Height="40" Fill="#0000FF"/>
    <Rectangle x:Name="LeftChild" Height="40"
               HorizontalAlignment="Left" Fill="#00FFFF"/>
  </StackPanel>

  <!-- Closure C (S829 — measure-entry): a Collapsed sibling is SKIPPED by
       Measure (its dirty bit is kept and its constraint re-armed,
       UIElement.cs:601-611) so it contributes 0 to the panel, and the reveal
       re-measures it through WPF's own signal path — the Visibility transition
       (enabled → ensureVisible → signalDesiredSizeChange,
       UIElement.cs:2984-3010/3043-3056) → OnChildDesiredSizeChanged → parent
       InvalidateMeasure (UIElement.cs:323-330). NO harness-side invalidate is
       used to demonstrate it: assert_desired_size propagation IS the closure. -->
  <StackPanel x:Name="TogglePanel" Background="#D0D0D0">
    <Rectangle x:Name="CollapsedSibling" Height="40" Fill="#FF0000"
               Visibility="Collapsed"/>
    <Rectangle x:Name="VisibleSibling" Height="40" Fill="#00FF00"/>
  </StackPanel>
</StackPanel>
